    "description": "Rotary piston water meters type PD97TRP designed to measure, memorise and display the volume at metering conditions of water passing through the measurement transducer. Semi positive displacement rotary piston water meters with wet mechanical indicating device with protected registered drums. Consist of a brass body (divided into two parts connected by screw) with connecting screw threads, an inlet strainer, a non return valve, a wet measuring unit with a piston and mechanical transmission, rubber O-ring, and a mechanical indicating device protected by a plastic cover, formed by numbered rollers with eight drums installed in a capsule filled with water and glycerine. Can be installed to operate in any position with the flow axis in the horizontal, vertical (from bottom to top and from top to bottom) and inclined plane, with the indicating device positioned at the top and at the side. Not designed to measure reverse flow. Can be equipped by a reed impulse transmitter for remote reading, which was not tested."
